Members the reference documents as raising on a value whose type is
certain from its assignments (diag.invalid_native_member, warning, on
the member): :Count and :Append() on an array literal, :Split() on a
string, a case-misspelled date property (:year), an SSL-object member
on a number (:ToJson()), and -- on a string.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Probe;
	:DECLARE aItems, sText, dToday, nNum, vOut;
	aItems := {1, 2, 3};
	sText := "a,b";
	dToday := Today();
	nNum := 4;
	vOut := aItems:Count;
	aItems:Append(4);
	vOut := sText:Split(",");
	vOut := dToday:year;
	vOut := nNum:ToJson();
	sText--;
	:RETURN vOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Probe;
	:DECLARE aItems, sText, dToday, nNum, vOut;
	aItems := {1, 2, 3};
	sText := "a,b";
	dToday := Today();
	nNum := 4;
	vOut := aItems:Count;
	aItems:Append(4);
	vOut := sText:Split(",");
	vOut := dToday:year;
	vOut := nNum:ToJson();
	sText--;
	:RETURN vOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
7:17-7:22 warning invalid_native_member: ':Count' on an array raises at run time: arrays have no Count property; use ALen() or :Length
8:9-8:15 warning invalid_native_member: ':Append()' on an array raises at run time: arrays have no Append method; use AAdd()
9:16-9:21 warning invalid_native_member: ':Split()' on a string raises at run time: the native Split is not reachable; use BuildArray()
10:17-10:21 warning invalid_native_member: ':year' on a date raises at run time: native members are case-sensitive; write Year
11:15-11:21 warning invalid_native_member: ':ToJson()' on a number raises at run time: SSL values have no ToJson(); use the ToJson() function
12:2-12:9 warning invalid_native_member: '--' on a string raises at run time: -- works on numbers and dates only
